-- title:
--   No n-torsion in higher principal units when v(n)<k
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`. Let $n$ and $e$ be natural numbers such that the principal ideal generated by the image of $n$ in $R$ equals $\mathfrak m^{e}$, i.e. $(n) = \mathfrak m^{e}$, and let $k$ be a natural number with $e < k$. Let $\zeta$ be a unit of $R$ lying in `principalUnits R k`, that is, a unit whose image in $R$ satisfies $\zeta - 1 \in \mathfrak m^{k}$ (this carrier condition is the definition of the subgroup `principalUnits R k` of $R^\times$), and suppose $\zeta^{n} = 1$. The conclusion is that $\zeta = 1$. Equivalently: for $k$ strictly larger than the valuation $e$ of $n$, the $k$-th principal unit group of $R$ contains no nontrivial $n$-torsion. No primality assumption on $n$, and no completeness assumption on $R$, enters.
--
--   This is the standard statement that the higher principal unit groups $U^{(k)}$ of a discrete valuation ring are torsion-free away from the ramification bound $k > v(n)$; for $n$ a prime it says that $n$-th roots of unity in $R$ are not congruent to $1$ beyond level $v(n)$. It is used in the computation of the index of the $n$-th power subgroup of $R^\times$ ([`IsDiscreteValuationRing.index_range_powMonoidHom_units_eq`](thm.html#IsDiscreteValuationRing.index_range_powMonoidHom_units_eq)) and in the local ramification analysis of principal units.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_eq_one_of_pow_eq_one_of_mem_principalUnits.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LocalRing_PrincipalUnits

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
